{"Title":"An Act expanding the powers of the town of Brookline to delegate licensing authority","BillNumber":"S1281","DocketNumber":"SD664","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"CSC0","Name":"Cynthia Stone Creem","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CSC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T16:29:52.187"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"CSC0","Name":"Cynthia Stone Creem","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CSC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T16:29:52.1866667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1281/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Creem, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1281) of Cynthia Stone Creem (by vote of the town) for legislation to amend section 5 of chapter 270 of the Acts of 1985, as amended, to authorize delegation by general by-law of all select board licensing authority.  Municipalities and Regional Government.  [Local Approval Received.]","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Chapter 270 of the acts of 1985 is hereby amended by striking out section 5 and inserting in place thereof the following section:-\r\n\tSection 5. Notwithstanding chapters 138, 140 or 148 of the General Laws or any other general or special law to the contrary, the town may, through its by-laws, delegate any licensing authority.\r\n\tSECTION 2. This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[{"Description":"SD664 -- Brookline","DownloadUrl":"http://malegislature.gov/api/DownloadReport?attachmentId=16096&title=SD664%20--%20Brookline"}],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J10","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J10"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J17","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J17"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}